  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nI will implement a novel quadrature-based optimization algorithm called \"Harmonic Projection Optimization\" that directly minimizes the overlap integral C5 through a two-stage process:\n   - **Stage 1**: Project the problem onto a harmonic basis using discrete sine and cosine transforms\n   - **Stage 2**: Apply constrained global optimization using EQAOA (Efficient Quantum-inspired Adaptive Optimization Algorithm) on the projected variables\n   This approach directly addresses the non-convex nature of the problem by leveraging:\n\n   \u2022 Orthogonal decomposition via SCT (Symmetric Canonical Transform)\n   \u2022 Bilevel optimization between frequency magnitudes and DC components\n   \u2022 Dynamic penalty functions to handle both integral and box constraints\n   - The rationale is that problems with periodic patterns and shift invariances often exhibit compressibility in frequency domain, along with theoretical evidence suggesting that minimal overlap solutions should have controlled Fourier coefficients\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   Variables: n-dimensional continuous variables w \u2208 \u211d\u1d4f using S-transform coordinates\n   Objective: minimize C5(w) = max{ (1/N) \u03a3|i|\u2264N/2 |\u27e8w,\u03c6_i\u27e9|\u00b2 } \n   where \u03c6_i are the Fourier basis functions \u03c6_i(x) = sin(\u03c0i x/L) + cos(\u03c0i x/L)\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Integral constraint: \u03a3w_i * (L/N) = 1/2\n   - Box constraints: 0 \u2264 w_i \u2264 (1/2) * (L/N)\n\n   Formulation in S-transform space:\n   - Slepian transform to find spatial-temporal basis functions\n   - Binaural cross-correlation coefficient as primary optimization metric\n   \n   Optimality conditions are defined via:\n   - Augmented Lagrangian for integral constraints\n   - Projected gradient methods for box constraints\n   - Maximum direction condition in frequency space\n\n   This formulation preserves the original problem's conditions while enabling vectorization and parallel computation, with explicit guarantees:\n\n   - All candidate vectors satisfy 0\u2264h[i]\u22641\n   - Sum(h)*dx=1 by design\n   - Periodicity and invariance properties are maintained\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   Initialization:\n   - Start with initial_h_values transformed to S-transform domain\n   - Compute base frequencies F0 = floor(n/8)\n\n   Phase A: Frequency decomposition (time budget 100s)\n   - Apply Symmetric Canonical Transform (SCT)\n   - Prune negligible frequency components (|f_j| < 1e-4)\n   - Compute adaptive frequency weights w_j = |f_j|^\u03b2 + 1e-5\n   \n   Phase B: Bilevel optimization (time budget 800s)\n   - Upper level: Minimize max_overlap subject to total_freq_perim = target_dist\n   - Lower level: Improve local minima via gradient descent on embedding space\n   \n   AdaptiveAnchorFinder():\n     Uses energy based selection of central frequencies:\n       sorted_idx = np.argsort(X_train[:,0])\n       return sorted_idx[range(0, n, len(X_train)//4)][::-1]\n\n   Implementation structure:\n   def optimize_h(n_init, fd_param, budget_remaining):\n     global h_current, h_best, n_best, phase_start_time, c5_history\n     # Phase initialization\n     n_0 = n_init\n     h = initial_h_values[:n_init].copy()\n     ...\n     (Implementation continues with detailed mathematical transforms and optimization loops)\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n   Controls: [-2.5, -2.0, -1.5, -1.0]\n   Tunable parameters:\n   - Fourier back-projection factor \u03b1 \u2208 (0.8,0.95)\n   - Bilevel coupling strength \u03b2 \u2208 (0.2,0.5)\n   - Spatial frequency band pass [low,high] = [1, floor(n/8)]\n   Adaptive steering rules:\n     Revert to simpler transforms (FFT-based) if variance > 3.0 or gradient > 5.0\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   Phase Budgets:\n   - Core Fitting: n=400 -> 600s\n   - Refinement: n=800 -> 400s\n   - Final polish: n=1600 -> 300s\n   Total: 1300s\n\n   Time management:\n     Checkpointing every 120s:\n        save_best_to_json(h_best, best_score)\n   Graceful degradation:\n        Reduce FT complexity if n>16 and budget<200s\n        Convert to Chebyshev polynomials when c5_history improvement < 1e-6\n\n6. Validation and return contract Checks:\n    - Integral: abs(sum(h) - n/2) < 2e-4\n    - Box constraints: all(h >= 0; h<=1)\n    - Valid score: c5_bound \u2264 current_best (which is dynamically updated)\n    Return format:\n        (h_values (possibly double-integrated), c5_bound, n_points)\n    with filter that rejection of any candidate not meeting:\n        c5_bound < previous_best * 0.995\n    Consistent with official evaluator",
